      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Right to Repair movement is essential because it breaks monopolies that artificially limit consumers to only one brand for repairs, effectively creating \"electronic walled gardens.\" By allowing independent technicians and using third-party parts, this advocacy empowers buyers with more control over their devices and significantly lowers long-term costs. Ultimately, supporting this shift transforms the narrative from corporate privilege to genuine consumer empowerment in the digital age.",
